 any major MUNI lines. More information at\nPrice: Free\nCategories: commun
 ity\, free\nSource: funcheap/san-francisco\n\nIf ever there was a time to 
 create our own history rather than let malevolent people write it for us\,
  that time is now! Meet the people and groups helping build a world that s
 erves everyone at the Howard Zinn Book Fair\, Sunday\, December 6\, from 1
 0am to 6pm\, at the San Francisco City College Mission Campus\, 1125 Valen
 cia Street. This year’s theme is A Time of Monsters\, A Time to Fight. T
 he Howard Zinn Book Fair started in 2014 as an annual celebration and this
  year features 40 panel discussions by authors and activists and a big roo
 m full of independent presses\, community groups\, artists\, and non-profi
 ts. All of our participants focus on empowering people to become engaged i
 n the struggle for a truly participatory and democratic society. We live i
 n a time when many are asked to survive what can only be called monstrous:
  authoritarianism\, war\, state violence\, environmental destruction\, eco
 nomic insecurity\, forced displacement\, attacks on civil rights\, and the
  everyday cruelties of systems built to dehumanize. But throughout history
 \, ordinary people have resisted monstrous situations and individuals in o
 rder to take more control of their future. This year we have dozens of spe
 akers in
LOCATION:is close to 24th and Mission BART and many major MUNI lines. More
  information at
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-free-howard-zinn-book-fair-40-panels-autho
 rs-activists-2026/
